1
00:00:00,198 --> 00:00:02,238
(Raj:)I had no idea

2
00:00:02,235 --> 00:00:03,935
(Raj:)tortilla chips were
such a good fuel source.

3
00:00:03,937 --> 00:00:07,837
(Leonard:)They're basically pure
hydrocarbons soaked in fat.

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,810
(Leonard:)Let's hope the lug nut expands.

5
00:00:09,809 --> 00:00:12,039
(Sheldon:)What if that burning
food attracts animals?

6
00:00:12,045 --> 00:00:14,175
(Howard:)We have plenty of food
for the animals.

7
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:15,550
(Bernadette:)We do?
WOLOWITZ: Yep.

8
00:00:15,548 --> 00:00:18,248
(Howard:)A six-foot wiener
in a Flash T-shirt.

9
00:00:18,251 --> 00:00:20,681
(Sheldon:)That's not very nice.

10
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,557
(Leonard:)It's a bachelor party.
Lighten up.

11
00:00:24,456 --> 00:00:26,796
(electric crackling)

12
00:00:27,593 --> 00:00:30,593
(Sheldon:)What is that awful smell?

13
00:00:30,597 --> 00:00:31,827
(Howard:)It's burning salsa.

14
00:00:31,831 --> 00:00:33,561
(Howard:)I'm hoping the acidity
and salinity

15
00:00:33,566 --> 00:00:35,636
(Howard:)combined with electricity
will corrode the lug nut off.

16
00:00:35,635 --> 00:00:38,165
(Sheldon:)What an innovative solution.

17
00:00:38,171 --> 00:00:41,611
(Sheldon:)Perhaps I don't give your
MIT education enough credit.

18
00:00:41,608 --> 00:00:44,078
Yeah, I saw it on Mythbusters.

19
00:00:45,944 --> 00:00:48,144
(metal scraping metal)

20
00:00:49,314 --> 00:00:52,054
(Sheldon:)All right, this rust,

21
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:54,851
combined with the aluminum
recovered from the van,

22
00:00:54,854 --> 00:00:56,454
(Sheldon:)is now thermite.

23
00:00:56,456 --> 00:00:57,456
(Leonard:)Great.

24
00:00:57,457 --> 00:00:59,587
Couple pinches
ought to do the trick.

